+### 6.7 The memory system's contract
+
+The memory system serves the tiles' requests on the request bus (3.3), with LPDDR behind it. This section specifies only what a tile sees: the packets that come back, their order, and what a program must keep to. Its internals (its cache, LPDDR scheduling, the write-token scheduler, and how it shares C&C's port with C&C's controller) are out of scope (section 7; item 9).
+
+**Where it sits.** The memory system is owned by C&C and, in v1.1, **served at C&C's port**: its packets enter the mesh through tile 0's "from C&C" route block with **src 64** (4.16), and a tile's write stream goes to **dst 64**. Address 65 is reserved for it, should it get a port of its own (2.1). It sends only modes 5, 8, 9 and 10, and, being a non-tile source, **nothing it sends is counted** (4.12).
