+
+**What a program must keep to** (invariant 17):
+- one outstanding request per tag, with its event consumed before the tag is reused (a write's token before its stream, so its ack cannot meet a pending token);
+- at most one read outstanding per replayer queue;
+- a write stream only after its token, covering its block exactly;
+- **no read outstanding and no write token pending across a group run**, so the memory system's traffic never meets the all-to-alls' schedule (4.16);
+- no read-port results outstanding while deliveries arrive (invariant 14, 4.3);
+- controller-memory deliveries inside controller memory and outside the mailbox (invariant 11).
